  Object cases Broad, Narrow have no valid discriminant.
  
  Runtime field "kind" in case Narrow has GADT constructors, whose type
  refinements are not supported in discriminator domains. Runtime field
  "value" overlaps between cases Broad and Narrow because number and number
  cannot be distinguished at runtime.
  
  Give every object case a required immutable field with the same JavaScript
  property name and distinguishable runtime values or types. A literal may
  precede a broader type only when the remaining payload fields have matching
  runtime names, types, optionality and mutability.